    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "To be (être)",
     "md": "**I am**, **you are**, **he / she / it is**, **we are**, **you are**, **they are**.\n\nFormes courtes : I'm, you're, he's, she's, it's, we're, they're.\n\nNégation : on ajoute **not** : She **is not** (isn't) a teacher.\nQuestion : on inverse : **Is** she a teacher ? — Yes, she is. / No, she isn't."
